verification_result:    2026-09-11 official runner R4 on 10.62.229.155 passed full conan create, package test, 100/100 torture, L0/L1/L2/L4/L5, and exited 0; PR CI #44737 downloaded all four sources through the mirror but stopped in generate() because sysroot was derived as native/llvm/ohos-sdk.org; PR CI #44804 then passed Conan test_package, L0, L1, cleanup, and all seven CI steps in 3781 seconds; PR CI #44812 reached L0 but the single GCC source connection timed out at 3600 seconds, so the recipe added bounded parallel Range downloads with ordered mirrors and final SHA256 verification; PR CI #44864 reached GCC all-gcc and printed 7,676,387 selftest pass(es) but timed out because build_jobs() returned 1 in the OHOS profile; PR CI #44912 verified the -j2 recipe reached the end of all-target-libgcc but still exhausted 3600 seconds; PR CI #44956 repeated the same all-target-libgcc boundary with -j4; PR CI #44992 removed decimal/BID objects and reduced the timeout by 193 seconds but still showed libgcc -g injection at the same boundary; PR CI #45033 then passed with LIBGCC2_DEBUG_CFLAGS=-g0, conan-build-test 3562 seconds, total 3647 seconds, Conan test_package, L0/L1, and all seven CI steps successful while retaining bounded pipe parallelism and the file:// source-cache path
current_blocker:        no current CI blocker; local Windows conan command remains unavailable because conan is not on PATH, which only limits local orchestration
